    "headline": "Anthropic files to go public on the Nasdaq under the symbol “ANT”",
    "summary_short": "Anthropic has filed its IPO prospectus with the SEC and will list on the Nasdaq as “ANT”. It gets ahead of OpenAI and discloses its accounts for the first time.",
    "summary_long": "Anthropic, the maker of Claude, has filed its S-1 with the SEC, the US securities regulator. It is the document that opens its IPO on the Nasdaq under the symbol “ANT”. It has not yet set the number of shares or the price. Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley are handling the offering. The company had already filed confidentially in June.\n\nThe 335-page prospectus devotes about 100 pages to risks. According to The Verge, it lost $80.7 billion in the first half on revenue of $16.3 billion. It also admits that its data centers increasingly depend on natural gas, which exposes it to rising fuel prices. MIT Technology Review questions its narrative: it presents itself as an AI safety organization and, at the same time, as a large company racing to get there first.",
